--- !u!114 &463664742
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 463664740}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3cd2b6b9237de174790754a1198b8eb2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  tutorialPanel: {fileID: 1880686524}
  tutorialText: {fileID: 1880686528}
  nextButton: {fileID: 1880686527}
  nextButtonText: {fileID: 1880686526}
  tutorialSteps:
  - stepText: Choose a planet you want to travel to from the galaxy map. Each planet
      is a new level with unique terrain, enemies, and crystal locations. Tap on
      a planet to start your mission.
    objectsToActivate: []
    objectsToDeactivate: []
  - stepText: Once you land, control your robot to explore the area. Move around
      the level and look for glowing crystals. When you find one, approach it and
      let the robot mine it automatically. Collect all the crystals on the planet
      to complete the mission.
    objectsToActivate: []
    objectsToDeactivate: []
  - stepText: Be careful - enemies patrol the area. If an enemy spots you, run away
      and avoid contact. Use the environment and your speed to escape and stay safe
      while continuing to collect crystals.
    objectsToActivate: []
    objectsToDeactivate: []
  - stepText: After you collect all the crystals, a takeoff button will appear on
      the screen. Tap this button to leave the planet and safely return to space.
    objectsToActivate: []
    objectsToDeactivate: []
  - stepText: Back in the hub, spend the money you earned from crystal mining to
      upgrade your character and robot. Improve speed, mining power, and survivability
      to make future missions easier.
    objectsToActivate: []
    objectsToDeactivate: []
  - stepText: You can also use your earned money to unlock new planets. Each new
      level offers greater rewards and more danger, so upgrade wisely before moving
      on.
    objectsToActivate: []
    objectsToDeactivate: []
